usage: inflate <command> <file>

decompress gzip, zlib or raw DEFLATE (detected, or
named by --gzip, --zlib or --raw after the verb):
  cat FILE        the data, if it is text
  cat FILE -o OUT write the data to OUT
  hex FILE        the data as hex, 32 bytes a line
  info FILE       header fields, sizes, checksums
  blocks FILE     one line per DEFLATE block
  bench FILE N    decompress N times, print a size
compress (fixed codes, LZ77), as hex or to OUT:
  gzip FILE [-o OUT] | zlib ... | deflate ...
  roundtrip FILE  compress three ways, decompress
checksums of the file as it is:
  crc32 FILE | adler32 FILE
[exit 2]
